Description: An independent native R mirror of the 'msprime' simulator
    <https://tskit.dev/msprime/> (not an official upstream release), for
    simulating ancestral histories
    (coalescent with recombination, gene conversion, multiple merger
    coalescents, selective sweeps, discrete-time Wright-Fisher and fixed
    pedigree models) under flexible demographic models, and for simulating
    mutations under a variety of mutation models, as described in
    Baumdicker et al. (2022) <doi:10.1093/genetics/iyab229>. The package
    bundles the 'msprime' and 'tskit' C libraries and does not depend on
    Python. Results are tree sequences that can be written to the standard
    '.trees' format and used directly with the 'tskitR' package.
Maintainer: Giovanny Covarrubias-Pazaran <cova_ruber@live.com.mx>
